WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.267
-We all love our pets.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.033
And every pet owner thinks
that their pet is the best.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.501
And I wanted to see
if that was true.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.868
So, it's time for "Why Is
Your Pet Better Than Me?"

00:00:07.868 --> 00:00:08.968
Here we go.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.434
-♪ Why is your pet
better than me? ♪

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:12.901
♪ Better than me ♪

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.901
Alright.
Let's meet our first pet.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.834
Hello.
Welcome to the show.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.934
What is your name,
and where you from?

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:23.934
Hello.
-Hi, Jimmy.

00:00:23.934 --> 00:00:25.133
My name's Christa.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:27.300
My husband, Michael,
is behind me.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.834
He's our ringmaster.
-Hi, Michael.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.234
-And this is Roo.

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:31.701
-Roo, welcome to the show.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.634
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:37.067
Christa, why is -- Is it Roo?
Is that the dog's name, Roo?

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.634
-That's her name, Roo.

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:39.767
-Her name.
Hi, Roo.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.501
You're very cute.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:45.434
She's ignoring me right now.
She's giving me full side eye.

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.901
Look -- That's right.
Aw, no.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:49.400
-Her attention fully on
what she's going to show you

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.968
right now, actually.
-Yeah, Roo.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:55.033
What does Roo do?
Why is your pet better than me?

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.200
-Roo is better than you
because she can keep balloons

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:00.167
up in the air
using only her nose.

00:01:00.167 --> 00:01:01.701
-Oh, yeah.
Let me see.

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:03.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.400
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.133
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.000
That is so good.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.167
Wow.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:13.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Roo!

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.801
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.234
I could watch that all day long!
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:21.767
Good job, Roo!

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.300
Oh, my gosh!

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.300
It's like she can't stop it!

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.567
It's unbelievable.
Love it, Roo!

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.200
Oh, my God, watch it all day.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.567
Thank you.
Great job.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.834
Thank you
for coming on the show.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.033
You're awesome.
I appreciate it.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.634
Thank you.
-Thanks for having me.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.567
-Let's meet our next pet.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:40.801
Hello. What is your name,
and where you from?

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:44.467
-My name is Roy Portner
from Abington, Pennsylvania.

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:46.100
Right outside of Philadelphia.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Outside of Philly.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.667
We love it.
Thank you.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.234
Roy, welcome to the show.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.701
Now, who do you have
there with you?

00:01:54.701 --> 00:01:57.267
-I have Marcus.
-Hi, Marcus.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:01.467
Hi, Marcus.
And what does Marcus do?

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:04.868
Why is he better than me?

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:07.901
-Marcus is better than you
because he can howl

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:10.868
the "Werewolves of London"
by Warren Zevon.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.067
-That's one of my jams.
I love Warren Zevon.

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.234
"Werewolves of London."

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.267
So that song comes on
and he howls to it?

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.601
-Yes, sir.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.501
Everyday, after I'm done
working, I'm ready to walk him.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.400
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.701
-All right, I got to here this.

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:24.334
Whenever you're ready,
go for it.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.868
[ "Werewolves of London" plays ]

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.200
-Sing it.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.167
[ Dog howling ]

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:35.934
-Yes!
My dude!

00:02:35.934 --> 00:02:37.133
Yes!

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.033
Yeah.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.534
Marcus, on his own terms.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.400
Great job.
-Took a while,

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.501
but we got him going.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:49.667
-Great job, Marcus!

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.534
Thank you for that.

00:02:51.534 --> 00:02:53.801
Alright.
Let's meet our last pet.

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.834
Hello. What is your name,
and where are you from?

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:59.400
-I'm Brad Friesen
from Vancouver, Canada.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.467
-Oh, Vancouver.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.267
Beautiful.
We love Vancouver.

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:05.434
And what is your dog's name?

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:06.868
-This is Mister Bentley.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.501
-Oh, Mister Bentley.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:12.467
Mister Bentley -- Why is
Mister Bentley better than me?

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.834
-Well, I've seen some
of your dance battles,

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.400
and you're not the best
moonwalker.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.300
And that's one of Bentley's
specialties.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.734
-I mean, yeah, I've done
the moonwalk a bunch of times,

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:23.901
one of my go-to dances.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.234
But Mister Bentley can moonwalk?

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.667
I don't think I've ever
seen a dog moonwalk.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.367
-Are you ready?
Go get it.

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.634
Get your ball.
Go get it.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.100
Yeah, he's got to go
get his stick.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.834
Get it.
You get it.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.000
Ready?
Get it.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.367
You get it.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:42.968
Got to come.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:45.133
♪♪

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:47.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:55.667
♪♪

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:56.834
-I'll take it!

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.234
We got it.

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:01.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.701
That's what I'm talking about,
a moonwalking dog.

00:04:03.701 --> 00:04:05.033
Thank you for being on the show.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:08.467
Good job, Mister Bentley,
good job.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:11.100
And great job to all
of our talented pets.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.033
If you have a pet that you think
is better than me,

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.234
I want to see it.

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:17.767
Go to tonight-show.com/
whyisyourpetbetterthanme

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.300
to submit a video of your pet.

